      <title>After the Minnesota surge, ICE is moving to a quieter enforcement approach</title>
      <link>https://www.ksfr.org/npr-news/2026-04-04/after-the-minnesota-surge-ice-is-moving-to-a-quieter-enforcement-approach</link>
      <description>ICE seems to be changing from aggressive immigration enforcement on city streets to an apparent return to operations that rely heavily on local law enforcement. But even in Florida, where sheriffs are required to cooperate with ICE, some conservative sheriffs have concerns about pursuing immigrants with no criminal records.</description>
